    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town of Pawlet was named for the Mettawee River, which appeared as Paulet or Paulette on early maps.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenerpasture.com/Places/Details/2681"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "West Pawlet sits in the valley of the Indian River, a tributary of the Mettawee River within the Lake Champlain watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Pawlet%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pawlet was one of the New Hampshire Grants, chartered on August 26, 1761, to Jonathan Willard and sixty-one shareholders.",
